From 70a14d2e285f98b848e0a2258bc05127d3b2e024 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: plotarmordev <299844489+plotarmordev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 03:26:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 14/18] nemotron: checkpoint prompt up kernels write down's
 NVFP4 rows

The prompt up tiles turn each relu^2 block of 16 into tf_ck_quant4's e4m3 scale and e2m1 codes from the same bf16
values, staged through shared memory and written out as whole rows (tf_ck4_up_nvfp4_prompt). Prompt passes no longer
write the bf16 up rows nor read them back to quantize; decode keeps its up kernels and quant4. `tf-cuda-test
checkpoint` compares the prompt rows with decode up followed by quant4 under a down input scale of 0.375.
---
 docs/recipes/nemotron-3.5-super-vl.md        |  5 +-
 zig/kernels/cuda/ck_experts.cu               | 92 +++++++++++++++-----
 zig/src/cuda/ck.zig                          | 11 ++-
 zig/src/families/nemotron/cuda_latent_ck.zig |  9 +-
 zig/src/families/nemotron/cuda_state.zig     |  6 +-
 zig/tests/cuda/ck_tests.zig                  | 14 +--
 6 files changed, 97 insertions(+), 40 deletions(-)

